<p class="prose">Engineering data arrives as a table: a property against a temperature, a section against a depth, a measured curve against a load. `linterp` reads a value out of one, interpolating linearly between the rows either side.</p>
<p class="prose">It carries units, which is worth saying because SMath's does not — its `linterp` reduces every entry to a bare number and hands one back, so worksheets that use it divide the units out by hand and multiply them back in. That form still works here; it is simply no longer necessary.</p>
